#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Causal liquidity-route day-trading research policy.

This is a structural replacement for the prior plan/RR lattice.  One causal auction
interaction can produce at most one trade plan.  Direction comes from the auction
outcome at a meaningful liquidity boundary; OB/FVG/SR-flip geometry only refines the
first defended return; the stop is the event invalidation; and the target is the nearest
still-live opposing liquidity pool rather than a fixed R multiple.

The research simulator uses future bars only to label an immutable plan.  A filled
position has no time exit: it resolves only at the predeclared target or stop.  The
four symbols share one global single-position account and every completed trade risks
3% of then-current NAV.
"""
